Id: time004w
Severity: WARN
Category: services
Check: check_timesync
Fix: Keep one daemon; systemctl disable --now the others.
References: chronyd(8); systemd-timesyncd(8)
Controls: CIS 8.4; NIST AU-8, SC-45; ISO 8.17

More than one time synchronisation daemon is running. Each corrects
the clock towards its own servers, so they fight, and the clock can
jump back and forth. It usually happens when chrony or ntpd was
installed on a system where systemd-timesyncd was already on.

To fix it, keep one and disable the others, for example 'systemctl
disable --now systemd-timesyncd' when chrony is the one to keep.
